     4.1.4 Expanding the formula into a multi-period dynamic model
    Examining the profit of an insurance company in a single year is not very meaningful. As
        微

                                           M


mentioned earlier, the insurance company can use the premiums collected in previous years to
pay out for the current year's insured insurance contracts. Therefore, we introduce a discounted
                                 ：




cash flow model to consider the long-term operating ability of insurance companies.
     We assume that the difference in discount rates in neighboring years is not significant, so
                           号




that the discounted cash flow rate is a fixed value over time. By discounting the insurance
