5 Task 2: Where should a property developer site buildings?




                                                                            型
5.1 Adjustment of the MDI model
     When building a new house, a property developer will inevitably face the problems of




                                                              模
“where to choose a site” and “how to choose a site”. Obviously, the lower the risk of damage to
the house, the more likely it is to be favored by property developers. Of course, low-risk land is




                                                             学
inevitably limited, and the purchase price of land will be higher; therefore, developers have to
focus on land with a certain level of risk, or even a higher level of risk. For this reason, property




                                                     数
developers usually purchase property insurance for their houses or hire organizations to
evaluate the level of risk the land faces, especially the probability of natural disasters.


                                       ：
     5.1.1 Describing the interaction between property developers and insurance




                                                                 els
companies
                                      号
     In the case of new housing construction, the decisions of property developers and insurance




                                                               od
companies interact with each other. On the one hand, the policies and insurance products of
                              众

insurance companies influence the choices of property developers. If the insurance company
                                                              m
charges too high a premium or chooses not to underwrite the policy, then the property
                       公


developer will face higher costs and take too much risk. On the other hand, property
                                                  H
developers' site selection decisions also have a potential impact on an insurer's earnings. A
                                               AT

property developer's community building policy affects the total amount of property in the area,
         信




which in turn affects the total amount of premiums received by the insurance company; at the
same time, the degree of disaster resistance of the houses designed and built by the property
        微

                                        M


developer determines the size of the loss that may be incurred by the corresponding houses
when they are exposed to the risk of a natural disaster, which affects the insurance company by
                                ：




affecting the frequency of insurance and the amount of claims, which changes the total amount
of compensation paid out by the insurance company. This all has an impact on the profitability
of the insurance company. Therefore, there is a strong interaction between property developers
                        号




and insurance companies.
                 信




1
  Slovakia has a high terrain, mostly located in the Western Carpathian Mountains, with small
plains in the southwest and southeast, and a higher mountainous area in the north, most of
         微




which is 1,000~1,500 metres above sea level. Slovakia has a temperate climate in the transition
from an oceanic to a continental climate, with a marked alternation of seasons. The average
temperature in the country is 9.8°C, with a maximum of 36.6°C and a minimum of -26.8°C. The
annual rainfall is 500~700 mm. Annual precipitation is 500~700 mm, with more than 1,000 mm
in the mountainous regions.
